# Notes App — Project Rules

## Architecture

### Data Model

```
interface NoteSummary {
  id: string;
  slug: string;
  title: string;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
  attachmentCount: number;
}

interface Note extends NoteSummary {
  content: string;
  attachments: Attachment[];
}

interface Attachment {
  id: string;
  originalName: string;
  mimeType: string;
  size: number;
  relativePath: string;
}
```

### Filesystem Layout

- Notes stored at `NOTES_ROOT/notes/YYYY-MM-DD-slug-uuid/`
- Each note folder contains `note.md` + `attachments/`
- Slug format: `${date}-${slugifiedTitle}-${uuid}`
- `NOTES_ROOT` configured via env var

### Core Functions (`lib/fsNotes.ts`)

```
listNotes(): Promise<NoteSummary[]>
getNote(id: string): Promise<Note | null>
createNote(input: {title: string, content: string}): Promise<Note>
updateNote(id: string, input: {title?: string, content?: string}): Promise<Note>
deleteNote(id: string): Promise<void>
listAttachments(noteId: string): Promise<Attachment[]>
saveAttachment(noteId: string, file: File): Promise<Attachment>
deleteAttachment(noteId: string, attId: string): Promise<void>
```

### API Routes

```
app/api/notes/route.ts              → GET, POST
app/api/notes/[id]/route.ts         → GET, PUT, DELETE
app/api/notes/[id]/attachments/route.ts        → GET, POST
app/api/notes/[id]/attachments/[attId]/route.ts → DELETE
app/api/notes/[id]/attachments/[attId]/download/route.ts → GET
```

- NextRequest/NextResponse
- Zod validation on every endpoint
- Error shape: `{ error: string }`

### Components

| Component | Location | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| MarkdownEditor | `components/MarkdownEditor.tsx` | `"use client"`, shadcn Textarea fallback |
| AttachmentList | `components/AttachmentList.tsx` | Card, Badge, Button |
| FileUpload | `components/FileUpload.tsx` | Drag & drop, Button, Card |
| ThemeToggle | `components/ThemeToggle.tsx` | `"use client"`, Button + lucide icons |
| NotesSidebar | `app/notes/NotesSidebar.tsx` | `"use client"`, sidebar with search + note list |

### Layout

- `app/notes/layout.tsx` — Server component: fetches notes, wraps pages in `SidebarProvider` + `SidebarInset`
- Mobile header with `SidebarTrigger` shown via `md:hidden`

### Pages

```
app/notes/page.tsx       → Empty state (no note selected)
app/notes/[id]/page.tsx  → Edit + upload
```

### Installed shadcn/ui Components

button, card, input, dialog, textarea, badge, sidebar, separator, sheet, tooltip, skeleton

## Rules

### Language

- All user-facing text (labels, buttons, placeholders, messages, tooltips, empty states) must be in German

### General

- Max 200 lines per file — split into smaller modules if exceeded
- TypeScript strict mode
- No database — filesystem only
- Tailwind responsive design
- `NOTES_ROOT` env var for data directory
- `revalidatePath()` after mutations
- Inline tests in every file
- File naming: PascalCase for components/pages, camelCase for lib/utils, lowercase for config
- Before writing any UI code, check `components/ui/` for an existing shadcn component first
- Never implement custom UI components from scratch. First check if a matching shadcn/ui component exists (`npx shadcn@latest add <name>`). Only build custom components when no shadcn equivalent is available.
- Run `bun run lint` and `bunx tsc --noEmit` after every code change. Fix all errors before moving on.

### Bun

- Use `bun install` instead of `npm i`
- Scripts: `bun --bun next dev`

### Style System (shadcn/ui + Tailwind v4)

- All colors defined as CSS variables in `app/globals.css` (`:root` for light, `.dark` for dark)
- Registered via `@theme inline` so Tailwind generates utility classes
- Dark/light mode via `next-themes` (class-based, `.dark` on `<html>`)
- ThemeProvider in `app/providers.tsx`, wraps app in `app/layout.tsx`
- `cn()` helper in `lib/utils.ts` for conditional class merging

**Color tokens:** `background`, `foreground`, `card`, `card-foreground`, `popover`, `popover-foreground`, `primary`, `primary-foreground`, `secondary`, `secondary-foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `accent`, `accent-foreground`, `destructive`, `destructive-foreground`, `border`, `input`, `ring`, `--radius`

**Component rules:**
- Use shadcn/ui from `components/ui/` for all interactive elements (Button, Card, Input, Dialog, Textarea, Badge)
- Import with `@/components/ui/...`
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
- Prefer CVA variants over inline Tailwind overrides when a component needs multiple visual styles
- Never use raw HTML elements when a shadcn equivalent exists
- Never hardcode colors — use semantic tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`)
- Never use `dark:` prefix — CSS variables handle light/dark automatically
- To add a color: define in `:root` + `.dark` in `globals.css`, register in `@theme inline`
- To add a shadcn component: `npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>`

### Approved Packages

```
@uiw/react-md-editor uuid zod gray-matter
shadcn/ui (via CLI)
next-themes radix-ui lucide-react
class-variance-authority clsx tailwind-merge tw-animate-css
```

### Never

- No database (Prisma, SQLite, etc.)
- No experimental Next.js features
- No wrong folder structure (see Architecture section)
- No external CSS frameworks (shadcn/ui is fine)
- No hardcoded colors (`bg-blue-500`, `#fff`, etc.)
- No `dark:` prefix for themed colors
- No new UI libraries without updating this file
- No custom styling that bypasses the design token system

## Docker

- Multi-stage `Dockerfile` using Bun
- `docker-compose.yml` with volume `./dev-notes:/app/data`
- See `README.md` for Synology deployment instructions
